---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How much does a website cost?",
    a: "Websites start from £200, and every website is quoted individually. Your quote sets out the total price and, if you'd like to spread the cost, the payment schedule we agree. Payments are by bank transfer, and no VAT is added because I'm not VAT-registered. Optional hosting and maintenance is a separate £25 a month.",
  },
  {
    q: "What happens once my website is paid for?",
    a: "It's yours. If I'm hosting it, hosting and maintenance carries on at £25 a month on a rolling basis until you cancel with one calendar month's notice by email. It includes hosting with HTTPS, technical maintenance, weekly backups of your website's code and files stored in its repository, and up to 30 minutes of minor content edits a month (unused time doesn't carry over). New pages, redesigns and new features are quoted separately. If you'd rather host it somewhere else, I'll give you a ZIP of the website files with basic setup instructions.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I have to pay for hosting while I'm still paying for my website?",
    a: "If I host it, yes: the £25 a month for hosting and maintenance starts when hosting starts, including while you're on a payment plan. It's a separate charge and doesn't count towards your website's price. You can use your own hosting instead and pay me no monthly fee. That doesn't change your website payments, and the website becomes yours once it's fully paid.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I pay off my website early?",
    a: "Yes. You can pay the remaining balance at any time, and the website is yours once it's fully paid.",
  },
  {
    q: "What if I cancel hosting and maintenance later?",
    a: "Give me one calendar month's notice by email. Hosting continues to the end of that month, which you pay for as normal. If your website is paid for, I'll send you a ZIP of its files and basic setup instructions before hosting ends, and tell you about anything that needs moving separately, such as a third-party service or account. Cancelling hosting never means losing a website you've paid for, and if you're still on a payment plan, those payments carry on as agreed.",
  },
  {
    q: "Who owns my domain and content?",
    a: "You do, whatever happens. If you already have a domain, you keep it. If you need a new one, I'll register it in your name and include up to £20 a year towards it while I host your website, including while you're on a payment plan. If a domain costs more, I'll agree the extra with you before buying or renewing it.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long does a website take?",
    a: "It varies by project, but most websites are ready within a few weeks of getting started, depending on how quickly content and feedback come together.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can you redesign my existing website?",
    a: "Yes. I can bring an outdated or hard-to-use website up to a modern, mobile-friendly standard.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need to provide the written content?",
    a: "Ideally yes, since you know your business best, but I'll guide you on what's needed and can help shape and tidy up the wording where it helps.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is included in the free homepage preview?",
    a: "A first look at how your homepage could feel and read, based on the information you share. There's no cost and no obligation to continue afterwards.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will the website work properly on mobile?",
    a: "Yes. Every Stapled. website is built mobile-first and tested across different screen sizes, since most local customers will find you on their phone.",
  },
];
---

<section class="faq section" id="faq">
  <div class="container faq__inner">
    <div class="faq__intro reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="faq__heading">Questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq__list reveal">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="faq__item">
          <summary>
            <span>{item.q}</span>
            <svg class="faq__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-muted">{item.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq__inner {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .faq__intro {
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }

  .faq__heading {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
  }

  .faq__item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
  }

  .faq__item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq__item summary span {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .faq__item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq__chevron {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .faq__item[open] .faq__chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .faq__item p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-right: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .faq__item p {
      animation: faq-in var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
    }
  }

  @keyframes faq-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(-4px);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }
</style>
